WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
SaveBench UX prototype. All contestants, designs, events and results are synthetic.
The challenge and shared criteria are inspected before starting the fixture.

00:04.500 --> 00:08.500
Run starts the built-in preview. Its original controls deliver recorded fixture events.
No model, game or backend trial is running.

00:08.500 --> 00:12.800
A1's factory diagram appears with its public plan and event feed.
The synthetic rod rate is 8 against a target of 10 items per game minute.

00:12.800 --> 00:17.400
The remaining fixture events introduce A2 and B1 sample results.
These illustrate the interface; they are not measured model performance.

00:17.400 --> 00:20.000
A2's retained result shows the later sample measurements.
Meeting these targets does not establish whole-factory optimality.

00:20.000 --> 00:23.300
Selecting older A1 restores that revision's diagram and retained result.
Its earlier shortfall remains visible after A2's sample success.

00:23.300 --> 00:27.000
Compare uses the latest tested fixture revisions, A2 and B1.
Locating B1 on the map reveals its different eight-building arrangement.

00:27.000 --> 00:31.300
The comparison separates observed design differences from the model's stated approach.
The sample sets thresholds, not a universal winning score.

00:31.300 --> 00:33.080
Game artwork was omitted at the capture boundary.
The displayed rectangles and routes are approximate prototype diagrams.
